sers/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-17T11:23:22Z","updated_at":"2025-08-17T11:23:22Z","body":"That is because the function itself is wrong. You cannot ignore .import files (that is partly why I mentioned the other issue), and you probably should not ignore .uid files.\n\nYou should also not hash the files before storing them, although I am actually not sure that part of the code is really doing anything. If the idea there is to encrypt or somehow obfuscate the files, the `add_file` method has an `ecrypt` param that should be used instead (the key is specified when calling `pck_start`).\n\n`PCKPacker` doesn't work like you would intuitively expect (like the export option in the editor). That is the other reason why I mentioned that issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3194320982/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3194903406","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109689#issuecomment-3194903406","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109689","id":3194903406,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-bltu","user":{"login":"Sasinim5","id":31878657,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODc4NjU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31878657?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5","html_url":"https://github.com/Sasinim5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sasinim5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T02:28:16Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T02:28:16Z","body":"> That is because the function itself is wrong. You cannot ignore .import files (that is partly why I mentioned the other issue), and you probably should not ignore .uid files.\n> \n> You should also not hash the files before storing them, although I am actually not sure that part of the code is really doing anything. If the idea there is to encrypt or somehow obfuscate the files, the `add_file` method has an `ecrypt` param that should be used instead (the key is specified when calling `pck_start`).\n> \n> `PCKPacker` doesn't work like you would intuitively expect (like the export option in the editor). That is the other reason why I mentioned that issue.\n\nHI, I did not ignore the files you mentioned. In my script, i already comment out them. about the hash, i did not hash file, just calculate the hash value. but maybe i hash the file by mistake, i will check it at tonight. thanks a lot for the info","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3194903406/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh"